<title>Curtin on migration: what 265 people told us</title>
<meta name="description" content="Results from the Curtin community conversation on migration, October 2026: three groups, where they still agree, and the changes people want most.">
<style>

:root{
  /* Kate Chaney MP's brand (katechaney.com.au): teal and navy, Barlow Semi Condensed and Inter.
     The three groups get their own colours, so none carries the MP's: amber for Group 1, a lighter amber for
     Group 2 (the two came out of one Polis group) and violet for Group 3. Dark mode has its own two ambers,
     below. Both sets pass the dataviz palette check against their map surface. */
  --fizz:#16A1B7; --on-fizz:#012253; --navy:#012253; --soft:#D3EFF4;
  --g1:#B45309; --g2:#E99A2C; --g3:#8547F0; --on-g2:#012253;
  --paper:#ffffff; --ink:#012253; --card:#ffffff; --muted:#4B5B73;
  --line:rgba(1,34,83,.14); --track:#E3E9F0; --tint:#E8F6F9; --deep:#012253;
  --display:"Barlow Semi Condensed","Arial Narrow",Arial,sans-serif; --text:"Inter","Helvetica Neue",Arial,sans-serif;
  color-scheme:light;
  box-sizing:border-box;
  padding-top:env(safe-area-inset-top,0px);
  padding-bottom:env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px);
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){
  :root:not([data-theme="light"]){
    --paper:#0B1629; --ink:#ffffff; --card:#14243C; --muted:#AFBBCC;
    --line:rgba(255,255,255,.16); --track:#2B3B55; --tint:#0F2C38; --deep:#010E22; color-scheme:dark;
    --g1:#9C4806; --g2:#C58719;
  }
}
:root[data-theme="dark"]{
  --paper:#0B1629; --ink:#ffffff; --card:#14243C; --muted:#AFBBCC;
  --line:rgba(255,255,255,.16); --track:#2B3B55; --tint:#0F2C38; --deep:#010E22; color-scheme:dark;
  --g1:#9C4806; --g2:#C58719;
}
*,*::before,*::after{box-sizing:inherit}
html{scroll-padding-top:env(safe-area-inset-top,0px);scroll-behavior:smooth;-webkit-text-size-adjust:100%}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){html{scroll-behavior:auto}}
body{margin:0;font-family:var(--text);color:var(--ink);background:var(--paper);font-size:18px;line-height:1.5;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased}
.wrap{max-width:77.5rem;margin:0 auto;padding:0 40px}
h1,h2,h3{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:600;margin:0;letter-spacing:-.01em;font-feature-settings:"lnum" 1}
p{margin:0}
a{color:inherit}
:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--ink);outline-offset:3px}
.btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:.95rem 1.5rem;border-radius:999px;font-weight:600;font-size:1.02rem;text-decoration:none;border:2px solid var(--navy);font-family:inherit;cursor:pointer}
.btn.solid{background:var(--navy);color:#fff}
.btn.line{background:transparent;color:var(--navy)}
.btn:hover{transform:translateY(-1px)}
.dot{width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:50%;display:inline-block;flex:none}
.dot.g1{background:var(--g1)} .dot.g2{background:var(--g2)} .dot.g3{background:var(--g3)}
.pill{display:inline-block;font-weight:600;font-size:.9rem;background:var(--navy);color:#fff;border-radius:99px;padding:.3rem .85rem}
q{quotes:"“" "”"}

/* ---------- hero ---------- */
.hero{background:var(--fizz);color:var(--on-fizz);overflow:hidden}
.hero :focus-visible{outline-color:var(--navy)}
.hero-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.05fr 1fr;gap:48px;align-items:center;padding:88px 0 100px}
.hero-text{container-type:inline-size}
/* the headline is three set lines, like the Warringah page's, sized to its column so they never rewrap */
.hero h1{font-size:min(14cqi,9vh,6.4rem);line-height:1.04;margin-bottom:30px}
.hero h1 .ln{display:block;white-space:nowrap}
.hero h1 .box{display:inline-block;background:var(--navy);color:#fff;padding:.02em .18em .06em;margin:.06em 0 .08em -.18em;border-radius:.07em;line-height:1.02}
.hero .turnout{font-size:.95rem;font-weight:500;margin-top:22px}
.hero .sub{font-size:1.4rem;line-height:1.45;margin-bottom:36px}
.hero .sub.intro{margin-bottom:.7em}
.actions{display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.sticker{width:8.25rem;height:8.25rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--navy);color:var(--fizz);display:grid;place-items:center;text-align:center;transform:rotate(-12deg);z-index:3;padding:0 .7rem}
.sticker b{display:block;font-family:var(--display);font-weight:700;font-size:2.1rem;line-height:1;margin:.1rem 0 .2rem;font-feature-settings:"lnum" 1}
.sticker span{display:block;font-size:.6rem;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2}
/* The hero's right side: one label per group (its size, name and a one-line description, linking down to its card)
   and the circle for what all three agree on, linking to the agreement section (Jack, 19 November 2026: no quote
   cards and no at-a-glance row). The labels are white in both modes, so their quieter text uses a fixed grey. */
.hero .cards{display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;position:relative;padding:0}
.hero .glabels{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px}
.hero .glabel{display:block;position:relative;text-decoration:none;color:var(--navy);background:#fff;border-radius:14px;
  padding:14px 44px 15px 22px;border-left:8px solid var(--gc);box-shadow:0 14px 30px -18px rgba(9,40,54,.55);width:calc(100% - 9.5rem)}
.hero .glabel small{display:block;font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.02em;color:#4B5B73;margin-bottom:2px}
.hero .glabel b{display:block;font-size:1.2rem;line-height:1.2;font-weight:700}
.hero .glabel em{display:block;font-style:normal;font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.35;color:#4B5B73;margin-top:3px}
.hero .glabel .chev{position:absolute;right:16px;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);font-size:1.15rem;color:#4B5B73}
.hero .glabel:hover b,.hero .glabel:focus-visible b{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}
.hero .glabel:focus-visible,.hero .sticker:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--navy);outline-offset:3px}
/* The circle sits against all three labels, on the right. Its ring is in bands like the labels: Group 1's colour on
   top, Group 2's at the sides and Group 3's underneath; "from 12deg" undoes the -12deg tilt so the bands stay level. */
.hero .sticker{position:absolute;right:-6px;top:50%;margin:0;width:10.5rem;height:10.5rem;transform:translateY(-50%) rotate(-12deg);
  border:7px solid transparent;text-decoration:none;
  background:linear-gradient(var(--navy),var(--navy)) padding-box,conic-gradient(from 12deg,var(--g1) 0 60deg,var(--g2) 0 120deg,var(--g3) 0 240deg,var(--g2) 0 300deg,var(--g1) 0) border-box}
.hero .sticker:hover{transform:translateY(-50%) rotate(-12deg) scale(1.03)}
@media (min-width:901px) and (max-height:53em){
  .hero .glabels{gap:12px}
  .hero .glabel{padding:11px 40px 12px 18px}
  .hero .glabel b{font-size:1.08rem}
  .hero .glabel em{font-size:.84rem}
  .hero .glabel small{font-size:.74rem}
}
/* Phones: the labels run full width and the circle follows them, centred */
@media (max-width:900px){
  .hero .glabel{width:auto}
  .hero .sticker{position:relative;top:auto;right:auto;transform:rotate(-12deg);align-self:center;margin-top:6px}
  .hero .sticker:hover{transform:rotate(-12deg)}
}
/* Short windows: keep the headline, lede and buttons on the first screen. See the README, "Layout".
   The space above the hero shrinks first; the headline's size also follows the window's height. */
@media (min-width:901px){
  .hero-grid{padding-top:clamp(28px,calc(100vh - 41.5rem),88px)}
}
@media (min-width:901px) and (max-height:47.5em){ .hero h1{font-size:min(14cqi,8vh,6.4rem);margin-bottom:22px} }
/* the hero sentence runs the whole column, so on short laptops, and on narrow windows that aren't tall, it steps down
   a size to keep the buttons on screen */
@media (min-width:901px) and (max-height:46em),(min-width:901px) and (max-width:70em) and (max-height:48em){ .hero .sub{font-size:1.1rem} }
/* Where the cards run well past the first screen, the headline starts level with them
   instead of sitting halfway down: very short windows, and narrow ones that are not tall. */
@media (min-width:901px) and (max-height:43.25em),(min-width:901px) and (max-width:62.5em) and (max-height:53em){
  .hero-grid{align-items:start}
}

/* ---------- sections ---------- */
section.block{padding:110px 0}
.head{margin-bottom:52px}
.head h2{font-size:clamp(3rem,5.6vw,5.4rem);line-height:.92;max-width:24ch}
#prio-h{max-width:none}
.head p{font-size:1.2rem;line-height:1.45;max-width:32rem}
.deep{background:var(--deep);color:#fff}
.deep .head p{color:#C8D3E2}
.tint{background:var(--tint)}

/* ---------- map ---------- */
.map-card{position:relative;border:2px solid var(--ink);border-radius:28px;padding:22px 26px 18px;background:var(--card)}
.map-top{display:flex;justify-content:flex-end;align-items:center;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px}
.map-hint .h-touch{display:none}
@media (hover:none){.map-hint .h-fine{display:none}.map-hint .h-touch{display:inline}}
#map .grp-name{fill:var(--ink);font-family:var(--text);font-weight:700}
#map .st-count{fill:var(--muted);font-family:var(--text)}
.gtop .big small{font-size:.5em;font-weight:600}
.someone{font:inherit;font-size:.95rem;font-weight:600;background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper);border:0;border-radius:99px;padding:.55rem 1.1rem;cursor:pointer}
#map{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;touch-action:manipulation;cursor:crosshair;overflow:visible}
#map .pdot{transition:transform 1.2s cubic-bezier(.2,.75,.2,1),fill .6s ease,opacity .6s ease}
#map .axis{stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:2}
#map .axis-label{fill:var(--ink);font-family:var(--text);font-weight:600}
#map .axis-note{fill:var(--muted);font-family:var(--text)}
.map-hint{font-size:.95rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:4px}
.map-lead{font-weight:600;font-size:1.05rem;margin-bottom:10px}
.person{position:absolute;z-index:5;width:21rem;background:var(--card);color:var(--ink);border:2px solid var(--ink);border-radius:18px;padding:16px 18px 14px;box-shadow:0 18px 40px -20px rgba(0,0,0,.5);font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.4;pointer-events:none;opacity:0;transform:translateY(4px);transition:opacity .15s ease,transform .15s ease}
.person.on{opacity:1;transform:none}
.person .pg{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;font-weight:600;font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:6px}
.person .pn{color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:10px}
.person .pn b{color:var(--ink);font-weight:600}
.person .pv{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:9px;margin-top:9px}
.person .pv q{display:block;margin-bottom:5px}
.ans{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-weight:600;font-size:.85rem;border-radius:99px;padding:.15rem .6rem;background:var(--track);color:var(--ink)}
.ans.a{background:var(--fizz);color:var(--on-fizz)}
.ans.d{background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper)}
.person .why{font-size:.82rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:10px}
.person .lean-h{font-weight:600;font-size:.88rem;margin:12px 0 7px}
.lean3{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto minmax(0,1fr) auto;align-items:center;gap:5px 10px;font-size:.84rem}
.lean3 .ln{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;white-space:nowrap}
.lean3 .lb{height:9px;border-radius:99px;background:var(--track);overflow:hidden}
.lean3 .lb i{display:block;height:100%;border-radius:99px}
.lean3 b{font-weight:600;text-align:right;font-feature-settings:"tnum" 1}
.person .note{margin-top:10px;font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.4}
.person .ex{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:9px;margin-top:10px}
.person .ex .exl{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;font-size:.84rem;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:4px}
.person .ex .exl .dot + .dot{margin-left:-3px}
.person .ex q{display:block}

/* ---------- group cards ---------- */
.groups-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);gap:24px;margin-top:48px}
.gcard{border-radius:28px;padding:30px 30px 30px;color:#fff}
.gcard.one{background:var(--g1)} .gcard.two{background:var(--g2);color:var(--on-g2)} .gcard.three{background:var(--g3)}
/* each card: its size and name, a label, then its statements side by side; Group 2's card shows where it sides
   with each of the other groups, in two columns, and the statement it backed more than both, across them */
.gcard .stand{font-weight:600;font-size:1.02rem;margin:0 0 12px}
.gcols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:16px}
.gcols.two{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}
.gcols .qbox{margin-top:0}
.gcol{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px}
.gcol.wide{grid-column:1/-1}
.gcol.wide .side{margin-top:8px}
.gcard .side{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin:0;font-weight:600;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.3}
.gcard .side .dot{box-shadow:0 0 0 2px #fff}
.qbox.wide{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.6fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:8px 28px;align-items:center}
.qbox.wide q{margin-bottom:0}
.gcard .pcts{flex-direction:column;gap:4px}
@media (max-width:900px){ .gcols,.gcols.two,.qbox.wide{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)} }
.gtop{display:flex;align-items:flex-end;gap:20px;margin-bottom:22px}
.gtop .big{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:600;font-size:6.4rem;line-height:.78;font-feature-settings:"lnum" 1}
.gtop .big .pc{font-family:var(--text);font-weight:600;font-size:.4em;vertical-align:top;position:relative;top:.12em;margin-left:.04em}
.gtop .who{font-size:1.1rem;line-height:1.3;padding-bottom:4px}
.gtop .who b{display:block;font-size:1.45rem;font-weight:600}
.qbox{background:var(--card);color:var(--ink);border-radius:18px;padding:18px 22px 18px;margin-top:12px}
.qbox q{display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:1.12rem;line-height:1.32;margin-bottom:12px}
.pcts{display:flex;gap:8px 20px;font-size:.95rem;flex-wrap:wrap}
.pcts span{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px}
.pcts b{font-weight:600}
.small-note{font-size:.95rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:22px;max-width:46rem}

/* ---------- common ground band ---------- */
.common{margin-top:64px;border-radius:28px;background:var(--tint);padding:34px 38px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr;gap:40px;align-items:center}
.common q{display:block;font-family:var(--display);font-weight:600;font-feature-settings:"lnum" 1;font-size:clamp(1.9rem,3vw,2.6rem);line-height:1.02;margin-top:14px}

/* ---------- dumbbells ---------- */
.dumb{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;margin-top:14px;overflow:visible}
.dumb .trk{stroke:var(--trk,var(--track))}
.dumb .rng{stroke:var(--rng,var(--ink))}
.dumb .tick{fill:var(--tk,var(--muted));font-family:var(--text)}
.dumb .ring{stroke:var(--ring,var(--card))}
.vals{display:flex;gap:8px 22px;font-size:.98rem;margin-top:8px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.vals span{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px}
.vals b{font-weight:600}
.nn{color:var(--muted);font-weight:400;font-size:.88em}
.half.agree .nn{color:#2C3E5A}

/* ---------- pairs ---------- */
.legend{display:flex;gap:26px;font-size:1rem;margin:0 0 32px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.legend span{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:9px}
.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;border-radius:28px;overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:28px;background:var(--card);color:var(--ink)}
.pair .topic{grid-column:1/-1;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:1rem;padding:26px 34px 0}
.pair .topic h3{font-size:2.6rem;line-height:1}
.pair .topic .n{font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap}
.half{padding:22px 34px 30px}
.half.split{margin:18px 0}
.half.agree{background:var(--soft);color:var(--navy);margin:18px 18px 18px 0;border-radius:20px;--trk:rgba(1,34,83,.18);--rng:var(--navy);--tk:#2C3E5A;--ring:var(--soft)}
.half.agree .pill{background:var(--navy);color:#fff}
details.all{margin-top:8px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.3);padding-top:18px}
details.all summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;font-size:1.05rem;padding:.2rem 0}
.all-list{list-style:none;margin:16px 0 0;padding:0;column-count:2;column-gap:44px}
.all-list li{break-inside:avoid;padding:12px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.18)}
.all-list q{display:block;font-weight:500;line-height:1.4}
.all-list .vals{color:#d3e2e8;font-size:.9rem;margin-top:4px;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px 16px}
.all-list .nn{color:inherit;opacity:.85}
@media (max-width:900px){.all-list{column-count:1}}
.half q{display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:1.32rem;line-height:1.3;min-height:3.9em;margin-top:14px}

/* ---------- section heads ---------- */
.head .head-line{margin-top:18px;max-width:42rem}

/* ---------- priorities ---------- */
.prio-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:24px}
.pcard{background:var(--card);border-radius:24px;padding:26px 26px 24px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;border:2px solid var(--ink)}
@supports (grid-template-rows:subgrid){.pcard{display:grid;grid-row:span 5;grid-template-rows:subgrid;row-gap:0}.pcard .echo{align-self:start}}
.pcard .rank{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:600;font-size:3.6rem;line-height:.8;margin-bottom:16px;font-feature-settings:"lnum" 1}
.pcard .tt{margin-bottom:22px;flex:1}
.pcard p.t{font-weight:600;font-size:1.16rem;line-height:1.3}
.pcard p.x{font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:8px}
/* each change leads with its net votes, which set the order; one bar on a shared scale (the top change is full width) */
.tally{margin:0 0 12px}
.tally .big{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:.45rem;margin:0 0 12px;font-family:var(--display);font-weight:700;font-size:3rem;line-height:1;color:var(--ink);font-feature-settings:"lnum" 1}
.tally .big span{font-family:var(--text);font-size:.95rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted)}
.tbar{height:10px;border-radius:5px;background:var(--track);overflow:hidden}
.tbar i{display:block;height:100%;border-radius:5px;background:var(--fizz)}
.pstats{font-size:.95rem;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.pstats b{font-weight:600}
.pcard .pstats{color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem}
.no-card{margin-top:28px;background:var(--navy);color:#fff;border-radius:28px;padding:34px 38px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:40px;align-items:center}
.no-card h3{font-size:3rem;line-height:.95;margin:0 0 14px;color:var(--fizz)}
.no-card p.t{font-weight:600;font-size:1.35rem;line-height:1.3;margin-bottom:14px}
.no-card p.s{color:#C8D3E2;font-size:1rem}
.no-card .tally .big{color:#fff}
.no-card .tally .big span{color:#d3e2e8}
details.rest{margin-top:28px;border-top:2px solid var(--ink);padding-top:18px}
details.rest summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;font-size:1.05rem;padding:.2rem 0}
.rest-list{list-style:none;margin:16px 0 0;padding:0}
.rest-list li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:3rem 1fr auto;gap:16px;align-items:baseline;padding:14px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
.rest-list .r{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:600;font-size:2rem;line-height:1;font-feature-settings:"lnum" 1}
.rest-list .t{font-weight:600}
.rest-list .s{font-size:.92rem;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap;display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:.6rem}
.rest-list .rnet{font-family:var(--display);font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);font-feature-settings:"lnum" 1}
.rest-list .rs{font-size:.9rem}

/* ---------- sub-headings, findings and echoes ---------- */
.sub-head{margin:88px 0 28px}
.head + .sub-head{margin-top:0}
.sub-head h3{font-size:clamp(2.4rem,4vw,3.6rem);line-height:.95}
.sub-head p{font-size:1.15rem;line-height:1.45;max-width:32rem}
.deep .common{color:var(--ink);margin:0 0 30px}
.harder{font-size:1.2rem;line-height:1.45;max-width:40rem;color:#C8D3E2;margin:56px 0 22px}
.harder b{color:#fff;font-weight:600}
.finding{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(1.9rem,3vw,2.6rem);line-height:1;margin:0 0 30px;max-width:46rem;font-feature-settings:"lnum" 1}
.echo{border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:18px;padding-top:14px}
.echo .el{font-size:.85rem;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:6px}
.echo q{display:block;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.38;margin-bottom:4px}
.echo .vals{font-size:.9rem;margin-top:6px}
.next{background:var(--fizz);color:var(--on-fizz);padding:110px 0;position:relative;overflow:hidden}
.next-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr;gap:48px;align-items:center}
.next h2{font-size:clamp(3.4rem,7vw,6.6rem);line-height:.9;margin-bottom:26px}
.next p{font-size:1.35rem;line-height:1.45;max-width:32rem;margin-bottom:34px}
.next .sticker2{justify-self:center;width:15rem;height:15rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--navy);color:var(--fizz);display:grid;place-items:center;text-align:center;transform:rotate(-10deg)}
.next .sticker2 b{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:700;font-size:3.6rem;line-height:.9;display:block}
.next .sticker2 > div{max-width:72%} /* keeps the wider Barlow words inside the circle */

/* ---------- how the priority vote worked ---------- */
.how{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:40px;align-items:center;background:var(--card);border:2px solid var(--ink);border-radius:24px;padding:26px 32px;margin-bottom:44px}
.costs{display:flex;gap:28px;align-items:flex-end}
.cost{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:10px;font-size:.92rem;text-align:center}
.cost b{font-weight:600}
.sq{display:grid;gap:3px}
.sq i{width:16px;height:16px;border-radius:3px;background:var(--fizz);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1.5px rgba(1,34,83,.6)}
.sq.s1{grid-template-columns:repeat(1,16px)} .sq.s4{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,16px)} .sq.s9{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,16px)}
.how p.cap{font-size:1.1rem;line-height:1.45;max-width:36rem}

/* ---------- how this worked ---------- */
.steps{list-style:none;margin:0 0 30px;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:20px}
.step{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;border:2px solid var(--ink);border-radius:24px;padding:24px 24px 26px;background:var(--card)}
.step .fig{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:600;font-size:3.8rem;line-height:.85;font-feature-settings:"lnum" 1}
.step h3{font-family:var(--text);font-weight:600;font-size:1.1rem;letter-spacing:0;line-height:1.3;margin-top:6px}
.step p{font-size:.98rem;line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}
details.fine{border-top:2px solid var(--ink);padding-top:18px}
details.fine summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;font-size:1.05rem;padding:.2rem 0}
details.fine .arows{margin-top:14px}

/* ---------- about rows ---------- */
.arows{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
.arow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,2fr);column-gap:32px;padding:24px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
.arow > p{grid-column:2}
.arow h3{font-family:var(--text);font-weight:600;font-size:1.12rem;letter-spacing:0;line-height:1.35}
.arow p{font-size:1.02rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:44rem}
.arow p + p{margin-top:.6rem}

/* ---------- notes + footer ---------- */
.notes{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:34px 40px}
.notes h3{font-family:var(--text);font-weight:600;font-size:1.08rem;letter-spacing:0;margin-bottom:6px}
.notes p{font-size:.98rem;line-height:1.5}
.links{display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:44px}
.links .btn{border-color:var(--ink);color:var(--ink)}
.links .btn.solid{background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper)}
footer{background:var(--navy);color:#fff;padding:48px 0 56px}
.foot{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:32px}
.foot strong{font-weight:600}
.foot .ack{color:#C8D3E2;font-size:.95rem}

@media (max-width:900px){
  .wrap{padding:0 20px}
  .hero-grid,.head,.groups-row,.pair,.no-card,.common,.foot,.sub-head,.next-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  .sub-head{margin:64px 0 20px}
  .how{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:20px;padding:22px}
  .costs{gap:20px}
  .arow{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:6px;padding:18px 0}
  .arow > p{grid-column:auto}
  .steps{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:14px}
  .step{padding:20px}
  .step .fig{font-size:3rem}
  .next{padding:72px 0}
  .next .sticker2{width:10.625rem;height:10.625rem}
  .next .sticker2 b{font-size:2.6rem}
  .hero-grid{padding:28px 0 64px;gap:28px}
  .hero h1{font-size:min(14cqi,3.6rem)}
  .hero .sub{font-size:1.2rem}
  .hero .turnout{margin-top:16px}
  .hero .cards{gap:16px;padding:6px 4px 10px}
  section.block{padding:72px 0}
  .head{gap:18px;margin-bottom:32px}
  .gtop .big{font-size:4.6rem}
  .gcard{padding:24px 20px}
  .map-card{padding:16px 14px 14px;border-radius:22px}
  .person{position:static;width:auto;opacity:1;transform:none;margin-top:12px;box-shadow:none;display:none}
  .person.on{display:block}
  .half.agree{margin:0 14px 14px}
  .half.split{margin:6px 0 0}
  .pair .topic{padding:22px 22px 0;flex-wrap:wrap}
  .pair .topic h3{font-size:2.2rem}
  .half{padding:18px 22px 24px}
  .half q{min-height:0}
  .common{padding:26px 22px;gap:18px}
  .prio-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  .no-card{padding:28px 22px;gap:22px}
  .notes{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  .rest-list li{grid-template-columns:2.4rem 1fr}
  .rest-list .s{grid-column:2;white-space:normal}
}
/* ---------- hover a card to bring it forward and fade the rest (mouse and trackpad only) ---------- */
@media (hover:hover) and (pointer:fine){
  .pair,.pcard,.no-card{transition:opacity .2s ease}
  #pairs:has(.pair:hover) .pair:not(:hover),
  #priorities:has(.pcard:hover) .pcard:not(:hover),
  #priorities:has(.pcard:hover) .no-card,
  #priorities:has(.no-card:hover) .pcard{opacity:.25}
}
@media (hover:hover) and (pointer:fine) and (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){ .pair,.pcard,.no-card{transition:none} }
@media (max-width:520px){ .steps{grid-template-columns:1fr} }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){ #map .pdot,.person{transition:none} .btn:hover{transform:none} }

/* ---------- RxC site shell (shared with the other project microsites) ---------- */
.rxc-shell{--ink:#17203A;--paper:#fff;--common:#EDFF38;--quiet:#5F657E;--hair:#D9DBE3;--voice-b:#E23A6B;
  font-family:"Bricolage Grotesque",system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--ink);background:var(--paper);font-size:15px;line-height:1.3;box-sizing:border-box}
.rxc-shell *{box-sizing:border-box;font-family:inherit;text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-size:inherit;line-height:inherit}
.rxc-shell a{color:inherit;text-decoration:none}
.rxc-shell a:hover{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.3em}
.rxc-shell a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #2B3EFF;outline-offset:3px}
.rxc-shell .wrap{max-width:78rem;margin:0 auto;padding:.75rem clamp(1.25rem,4vw,4.5rem);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap}
.rxc-shell.top{border-bottom:2px solid var(--ink)}
.rxc-shell.bottom{border-top:1px solid var(--hair);font-size:14px;color:var(--quiet)}
.rxc-shell.bottom a{color:var(--ink)}
.rxc-shell .crumbs{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;color:var(--quiet);min-width:0}
.rxc-shell .crumbs a{font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem}
.rxc-shell .crumbs span.here{overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;white-space:nowrap}
.rxc-shell .status{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.4rem;color:var(--quiet)}
.rxc-shell .status i{width:.5rem;height:.5rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--voice-b);display:inline-block}
.rxc-shell .status.done i{background:var(--ink)}
.rxc-shell .btn{border:2px solid var(--ink);padding:.45rem .8rem;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;line-height:1}
.rxc-shell .btn:hover{background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper);text-decoration:none}
.rxc-shell .right{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap}
.rxc-shell .btn{border-radius:0;background:transparent;display:inline-block}
.rxc-shell .btn:hover{transform:none}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="rxc-shell top" role="banner">
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="3" width="12" height="12"/><rect x="9" y="9" width="12" height="12"/></svg>RadicalxChange</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <a href="/projects/">Projects</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="here">Curtin on migration</span>
    </nav>
    <div class="right">
      <span class="status done"><i></i>Completed, October 2026</span>
      <a class="btn" href="mailto:info@radicalxchange.org?subject=Curtin%20migration%20results">Contact the team</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>


<header class="hero" id="top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-text">
        <h1><span class="ln">Curtin wants</span><span class="ln"><span class="box">a long-term plan</span></span><span class="ln">for migration</span></h1>
        <p class="sub intro">Multiculturalism is central to Australia’s story, identity and future. As debate over migration levels and settings continues, this process offers a more nuanced, participatory way for communities to give feedback on immigration policy.</p>
        <p class="sub">People disagree about how many should come, and how fast. But most want migration planned years ahead, with housing, roads, schools and hospitals keeping pace. A ten-year plan came first when people voted on priorities.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="btn solid" href="#groups">See what Curtin said</a><a class="btn line" href="#priorities">The changes people want most</a></div>
        <p class="turnout">8 to 27 October 2026 · 265 people took part · 232 in a group</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cards">
        <div class="glabels" role="list" aria-label="The three groups">
          <div role="listitem"><a class="glabel" href="#group-1" style="--gc:var(--g1)"><small>Group 1 · 118 people</small><b>Migration works</b><em>Migrants aren’t the housing problem; keep helping people in need.</em><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
          <div role="listitem"><a class="glabel" href="#group-2" style="--gc:var(--g2)"><small>Group 2 · 77 people</small><b>Works, but slower</b><em>Migration helps, but take longer and get the checks right.</em><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
          <div role="listitem"><a class="glabel" href="#group-3" style="--gc:var(--g3)"><small>Group 3 · 37 people</small><b>Fewer, chosen more carefully</b><em>Temporary visas shouldn’t lead to permanent residency.</em><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
        </div>
        <a class="sticker" href="#agree" aria-label="More than 3 in 4 people in all three groups want migration planned 10 to 15 years ahead. See where the groups agree."><div aria-hidden="true"><span>More than</span><b>3 in 4</b><span>in all three groups want migration planned 10 to 15 years ahead</span></div></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
<section class="block" id="groups" aria-labelledby="groups-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="groups-h">Most people fit into one of three groups</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="sub-head"><h3>Where everyone sits</h3></div>
    <div class="map-card" id="map-card">
      <p class="map-lead">Each dot is one person, placed by how they voted. People who voted alike sit close together, so the higher the pile, the more people voted that way.</p>
      <div class="map-top">
        <button class="someone" type="button" id="someone">Show me someone</button>
      </div>
      <svg id="map" viewBox="0 0 1000 560" role="img" aria-labelledby="map-desc"><desc id="map-desc">A map of 232 people, placed left to right by how they voted. Group 1, Migration works, 118 people, sits on the left, where people agreed that migration is working. Group 2, Works, but slower, 77 people, sits next to it: they see migration working too, but want it slower. Group 3, Fewer, chosen more carefully, 37 people, sits on the right, where people agreed that fewer migrants should arrive more slowly. Where many people sit close together, the dots pile up.</desc></svg>
      <div class="person" id="person" aria-live="polite"></div>
      <p class="map-hint"><span class="h-fine">Hover over a dot to see how that person voted.</span><span class="h-touch">Tap the map or press “Show me someone” to see how one person voted.</span></p>
    </div>
    <div class="groups-row">
      <div class="gcard one" id="group-1">
        <div class="gtop"><span class="big">1<small> in </small>2</span><span class="who"><b>Group 1: Migration works</b>118 people</span></div>
        <p class="stand">What sets them apart</p>
        <div class="gcols">
          <div class="qbox"><q>Migrants are not the problem with the housing market</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>89%</b> of Group 1 agree</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>41%</b> of Group 2 <span class="nn">(17 voted)</span></span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>15%</b> of Group 3 <span class="nn">(13 voted)</span></span></div></div>
          <div class="qbox"><q>Refugees need years of support to recover from trauma, so they shouldn’t be judged by the same standards as skilled migrants.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>96%</b> of Group 1 agree</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>53%</b> of Group 2 <span class="nn">(15 voted)</span></span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>32%</b> of Group 3 <span class="nn">(19 voted)</span></span></div></div>
          <div class="qbox"><q>As a lucky country, we have a duty to keep helping people who aren’t so lucky, even when it costs us.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>89%</b> of Group 1 agree</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>51%</b> of Group 2</span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>16%</b> of Group 3</span></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="gcard two" id="group-2">
        <div class="gtop"><span class="big">1<small> in </small>3</span><span class="who"><b>Group 2: Works, but slower</b>77 people</span></div>
        <p class="stand">Where they stand</p>
        <div class="gcols two">
          <div class="gcol"><p class="side"><i class="dot g1"></i>Like Group 1 · Migration works</p>
            <div class="qbox"><q>Migration has worked well and should be seen as a positive</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>86%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>98%</b> of Group 1</span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>19%</b> of Group 3 <span class="nn">(16 voted)</span></span></div></div>
            <div class="qbox"><q>Without migration the economic burden to provide for an ageing population will fall to fewer people.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>88%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>97%</b> of Group 1</span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>21%</b> of Group 3 <span class="nn">(19 voted)</span></span></div></div></div>
          <div class="gcol"><p class="side"><i class="dot g3"></i>Like Group 3 · Fewer, chosen more carefully</p>
            <div class="qbox"><q>The culture of my community is changing faster than people can adjust, and it’s fair to worry about that.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>76%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>11%</b> of Group 1</span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>84%</b> of Group 3</span></div></div>
            <div class="qbox"><q>Temporary visas should stay temporary. People who come on them know the deal, and staying on shouldn’t be expected.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>90%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>32%</b> of Group 1</span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>93%</b> of Group 3</span></div></div></div>
          <div class="gcol wide"><p class="side">More than both other groups</p>
            <div class="qbox wide"><q>I’d rather the system took longer and got the checks right than rushed decisions.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>79%</b> of Group 2 agree</span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>25%</b> of Group 1</span><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>60%</b> of Group 3</span></div></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="gcard three" id="group-3">
        <div class="gtop"><span class="big">1<small> in </small>6</span><span class="who"><b>Group 3: Fewer, chosen more carefully</b>37 people</span></div>
        <p class="stand">What sets them apart</p>
        <div class="gcols">
          <div class="qbox"><q>A temporary visa should not lead to permanent residency.</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>94%</b> of Group 3 agree <span class="nn">(17 voted)</span></span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>7%</b> of Group 1</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>39%</b> of Group 2 <span class="nn">(18 voted)</span></span></div></div>
          <div class="qbox"><q>We need net negative migration to ease housing and raise wages. Big business is funding mass migration and selling out Aussies</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>80%</b> of Group 3 agree <span class="nn">(15 voted)</span></span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>0%</b> of Group 1</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>6%</b> of Group 2 <span class="nn">(16 voted)</span></span></div></div>
          <div class="qbox"><q>Is there a native skills shortage requiring immigration or are we under investing in skills because it is cheaper to import them?</q>
            <div class="pcts"><span><i class="dot g3"></i><b>75%</b> of Group 3 agree <span class="nn">(12 voted)</span></span><span><i class="dot g1"></i><b>22%</b> of Group 1</span><span><i class="dot g2"></i><b>28%</b> of Group 2 <span class="nn">(18 voted)</span></span></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="small-note">The people who joined in aren’t a random sample, so these groups describe who took part, not all of Curtin. 33 people aren’t in a group: they voted on too few statements, or didn’t agree or disagree with any.</p>


  </div>
</section>

<section class="block deep" id="agree" aria-labelledby="agree-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="agree-h">Even where they disagree, they agree on something</h2>
      <p class="head-line">At least 7 in 10 people in every group agreed with 15 statements. Here are four of them, each beside a related statement the groups disagree on.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="pairs"></div>
    <details class="all">
      <summary>See all 15 statements all three groups agreed with</summary>
      <ol class="all-list" id="all"></ol>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block tint" id="priorities" aria-labelledby="prio-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="prio-h">The six changes people want most</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="how">
      <div class="costs" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="cost"><div class="sq s1"><i></i></div><p><b>1 vote</b><br>1 credit</p></div>
        <div class="cost"><div class="sq s4"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><p><b>2 votes</b><br>4 credits</p></div>
        <div class="cost"><div class="sq s9"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><p><b>3 votes</b><br>9 credits</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="cap">At a workshop on 14 October, 72 people used quadratic voting to spread a budget of credits across 13 possible changes, for or against. Each extra vote on the same idea costs more, so the totals show what people care about most.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="finding">In the conversation, most people in every group agreed with four of the top six.</p>
    <div class="prio-grid" id="prio"></div>
    <div class="no-card">
      <div><h3>And one clear no</h3><p class="t">Prioritise migrants in high-paying jobs, using salary rather than shortage lists to decide who qualifies.</p><p class="s">43 people opposed it and 13 backed it. Most of the opposition was mild, with one or two votes each.</p></div>
      <div><div class="tally"><p class="big">−74<span>net votes</span></p></div></div>
    </div>
    <details class="rest">
      <summary>See the other six changes</summary>
      <ol class="rest-list" id="rest"></ol>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head"><h2 id="about-h">How this worked</h2></div>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="step"><span class="fig">36</span><h3>Starter statements</h3><p>Kate Chaney’s team and RadicalxChange wrote the first statements to open the conversation.</p></li>
      <li class="step"><span class="fig">265</span><h3>People took part</h3><p>From 8 to 27 October they voted agree, disagree or pass, online or at a workshop on 14 October, and added statements of their own.</p></li>
      <li class="step"><span class="fig">3</span><h3>Groups emerged</h3><p>Polis, an open-source tool, grouped people who voted alike into two groups. One of them split clearly on several questions, so we show three. Nobody chose a group. We named them.</p></li>
      <li class="step"><span class="fig">72</span><h3>Voters set priorities</h3><p>On 14 October they spread a budget of credits across 13 possible changes, using quadratic voting.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <details class="fine">
      <summary>Notes for checking the numbers</summary>
      <div class="arows">
        <div class="arow"><h3>Reading the percentages</h3><p>Each figure is the share of a group who agreed, out of those in the group who voted on that statement. Later statements had fewer voters, so where fewer than 20 people in a group voted, we show how many. We apply the 7-in-10 bar before rounding, so a statement shown at 70% can still fall just short.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>Reading the map</h3><p>We rebuilt the map from the published votes using the same method as Polis, so it is close to the Polis report but not identical. Left to right is the main divide. Where many people sit close together, their dots pile up, so a dot can sit a little to one side of its exact place. How often each person agreed overall is on their card. Each person’s card shows up to three of their votes as examples, one for each group they voted like. For each, it shows the statement most of that group agreed with (or rejected), judged cautiously when few people voted, preferring statements the person agreed with over ones they rejected. A statement that fits two groups is shown once.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>How we found three groups</h3><p>Polis, the tool that grouped people, found two groups. Inside the larger one, people split clearly on several questions, so we show them as two groups. That makes three.</p><p>Group 2’s 77 people sit nearest the border with Group 3, and differ from Group 1’s 118 on 14 statements. On each, at least 65% agreed on one side and at most 35% on the other, with at least 10 people voting on each side, and a gap that big would happen by chance less than once in a thousand times.</p><p>Eight of them had at least 20 people voting on each side. A community’s culture changing faster than people can adjust: 76% of Group 2 agreed, against 11% of Group 1. Temporary visas staying temporary: 90% against 32%. Taking longer to get the checks right: 79% against 25%. Capping permanent migration at what housing can take: 71% against 16%. Keeping the visa appeals process from becoming a pathway to stay: 90% against 34%. English and an understanding of our values for family members: 81% against 29%. Putting people who can work ahead of family reunion when places are limited: 70% against 34%. Not choosing the best if most permanent visas go to people already here: 67% against 29%. Nearly everyone in both groups backs a real path to stay for long-term residents: 97% of each.</p><p>Trying many split points and statements can turn up a few differences by luck. So we also put the members of Polis’s larger group in 1,000 random orders and ran the same search on each (a permutation test). It never found more than three such statements, and in 616 of the 1,000 orders it found none. The real order shows 14. Group 2 voted on a median of 40 statements and Group 1 on 70, enough to place them.</p><p>Inside Group 3, Polis’s smaller group, the same test found only one such statement, too few to split it. Random orders of its members found as many in 46 of the 1,000.</p><p>We also looked for unlikely allies, people in different groups who back the same statements, and found none that held up.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>The group cards</h3><p>The cards for Groups 1 and 3 show three statements most of the group agreed with and far fewer of both other groups did. Group 2 mostly sides with one or other of the groups beside it, so its card shows two statements where it sides with Group 1, two where it sides with Group 3, and one it backed more than both. RadicalxChange chose which statements to show.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>Who and what we counted</h3><p>419 statements were open for voting: the 36 starter statements and 383 written by people taking part. The moderators held back 118 others, so no one else voted on them.</p><p>We count the 265 people who voted on at least one of those 419 statements. Between them they cast 21,315 votes. Polis’s own count of 266 also includes one account whose only vote was on a statement of its own that the moderators held back.</p><p>One person voted on enough statements to be placed in a group, but didn’t agree or disagree with any of them: every vote they cast was a pass. They count as taking part, but we haven’t placed them in a group, because a pass doesn’t show where someone stands. Polis places them anyway, because it reads a pass as halfway between agree and disagree.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>Pairing the statements</h3><p>RadicalxChange chose which statements to pair. Every number comes straight from the results. People who took part online and at the 14 October workshop gave very similar results.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>The priority vote</h3><p>A separate vote with its own voters. We set aside ballots that used fewer than 10 credits. Where someone voted more than once, we counted the last ballot they submitted. That leaves 72 voters. Net votes are votes for minus votes against. The matching statements from the conversation are close in meaning, not identical in wording.</p></div>
        <div class="arow"><h3>The data</h3><p>From the Polis export of 30 October 2026, after voting closed on 27 October. Statements appear exactly as people wrote them.</p></div>
      </div>
