sa should not lead to permanent residency.","70":"Permanent migration should be capped at what our housing can accommodate.","73":"We should prioritise migrants from countries who are likely to assimilate into Australian society","86":"Why can’t family reunions can take place in the country of origin, why should the Australian taxpayer fund someone’s family to come here?","87":"Centrelink benefits, Medicare and other government support should only be allowed for verified refugees, not other immigrants.","95":"Migrants are not the problem with the housing market","96":"Migrants bring valued traditions to our communities","98":"Helping families reunite is an important part of a working migration shstem","103":"Without migration the economic burden to provide for an ageing population will fall to fewer people.","106":"People should have the rights to -access housing, education, healthcare that is funded by the government no matter where they’ve come from.","107":"If Australia had the infrastructure and resources for a larger population, would you support a higher net migration?","109":"The process for family migration, in particular for older parents joining their Australian citizen children needs to be quicker and clearer","122":"I don’t have a problem with genuine refugees provided they are vetted but I do have a problem with assylum seekers being given a free run.","123":"The migration debate seems to have become more racist and less trusted since cost-of-living became a real issue here.","131":"If there is a housing shortage, is immigration fuelling an increase in house prices and so the affordability crisi we hear about?","134":"Migration has worked well and should be seen as a positive","136":"ongoing suitability assessments of the migrant. Ensuring a growing assimilation by the migrant.","144":"Migrants have enhanced our culture and economy.","145":"International students should be required to leave Aust at the end of the qualification upon which the visa application was made.","165":"Migrant crime is a real issue and threatening to our way of life","169":"There are too many new migrants coming in we need to shut the gates and focus on remigration of the illegal ones","170":"Agree on government funding but also real value in hosting international students for business, for trade and for skills development","171":"Mass migration is destroying social cohesion, we need a 5 year pause on all migration","176":"Australians should not forget we are all migrants except for First Nations people as so deal with newer migrants humanely","178":"All too often migrants are blamed for the difficulties people experience during challenging times.","179":"Offshore detention should be abolished and asylum seekers should work in shortage areas while applications are processed","198":"Social benefits should only apply to citizens.","224":"Migrants on visas should have access to services like medicare","232":"There are innate differences between ethnicities which are currently not, but need to be considered to effectively plan an civilization.","249":"When bringing in people from trouble spots, we need to fund extra support to help them settle.","294":"the government needs to be extracting money from large multinational corporations not migrants and international students","390":"There is too much competition for homes to purchase and rent, this pressure and cost would be reduced with reduced migration","392":"Shelter is a basic human right, and if our kids cannot buy/rent their own homes, the immigration numbers need to be reduced drastically"},"nsplit":50,"cut":0.427};
